[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_7]
United protest: The Meterorite Incident

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_7_desc]
Recently, the Equestria Empire Ministry of National Security claimed that a meteorite fell at the border of Appleloosa and Rock Farm, cutting off the central railway transportation artery of Equestria.
Appleloosa suspected that this was a deliberate sabotage and planned to go to the target location for investigation, but the Ministry of National Security immediately dispatched a special action team to the area. The Empress ordered the investigation team of Appleloosa not to approach the area on the grounds of “protecting meteorites with magical research value”. The Ministry of Science and Magic has not responded to Appleloosa’s question of “why the Imperial Observatory of the Ministry of Science and Magic did not have meteorite observation records”, and refused to disclose the observation records on the grounds of “scientific research safety”.
Appleloosa immediately made a strong response, closing the border to the Empire. Now, they are asking us to cooperate to protest the Empire’s barbaric behavior together.

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_7_o0]
No problem!

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_7_o1]
Suggest Appleloosa to restrain

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_8]
Disturbed Empress

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_8_desc]
Breaking News! The Empress and her entourage were attacked by a group of unknown ponies while inspecting Appleloosa. As the Empress’s convoy turned into an alley, a group of masked ponies suddenly emerged from all sides and threw a large number of apple pies at the Empress, then quickly left.
The Empress was not injured as her bodyguards blocked most of the pies — though, her entire convoy was eventually buried under piles of pies. The Empress’s convoy was forced to end the inspection early. The Imperial Spokespony stated that the Empress was very angry about the attack and believed it was a threat from Appleloosa: due to the Meteorite Incident, the Appleloosa ponies have been protesting the Empire’s intervention recently, and the attack was likely carried out by the protesters, with the tacit approval of the Appleloosa authorities.
In response, “Cousin” Braeburn denied that the attackers were related to the protesters or Appleloosa, and promised to launch an investigation. Until the investigation results are out, he called for the Empress’s safety to be considered and for her never to visit Appleloosa again.

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_8_o0]
That’ll show her.

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_8_o1]
Outrageous!

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_8_o2]
Scary!

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_8_o3]
Emm...

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_8_TOOLTIP]
We will have an excuse to launch a punitive war against §Y[C14.GetName]§!
§RBut be aware that it will also involve [C12.GetName]§!

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_9]
The Meteorite Conflict

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_9_desc]
Yesterday, the Equestria Empire and the Appleloosa Autonomous Region ended the meteorite conflict with the victory of Appleloosa. The Empire signed an agreement with the leader of the autonomous region, “Cousin” Braeburn, and the special action team of the Empire as well as other garrisons will withdraw from the surrounding area of Appleloosa.
This Meteorite Conflict started when Equestria Empire Ministry of National Security claimed that a meteorite fell at the border of Appleloosa and Rock Farm, cutting off the central railway transportation artery of Equestria.
Appleloosa suspected that this was a deliberate sabotage and planned to go to the target location for investigation, but the Ministry of National Security immediately dispatched a special action team to the area. The Empress ordered the investigation team of Appleloosa not to approach the area on the grounds of “protecting meteorites with magical research value”. The Ministry of Science and Magic has not responded to Appleloosa’s question of “why the Imperial Observatory of the Ministry of Science and Magic did not have meteorite observation records”, and refused to disclose the observation records on the grounds of “scientific research safety”.
Subsequently, Appleloosa erupted in large-scale protests, and Appleloosa forcibly sent troops to the target location, immediately engaging in a firefight with the Empire’s special action team.
Now that the conflict has ended, we still do not know the truth of the event: does the meteorite really exist?

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_9_o0]
Great victory!

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_9_o1]
This is not over

[en.EVENT_C14_MAIN_9_o2]
Emm...

